2301:
(a) Suppose X has a gamma distribution with parameters \(\alpha\) and \(\beta\) having the probability
function \(f(x) = 

$$
\begin{cases}
\frac{1}{\Gamma\alpha \beta^\alpha} x^{\alpha-1} e^{-\frac{x}{\beta}}, & x > 0 \\ 0, & elsewhere
\end{cases}
$$

\) where \(\Gamma\alpha = (\alpha - 1)!\)
Show that \(E(X^k) = \frac{\Gamma(\alpha+k)}{\Gamma\alpha}\beta^k\) where k is a positive integer. Hence find the mean and variance of X **(10 Marks)**



(b) Suppose X has a beta distribution with parameters \(\alpha\) and \(\beta\) having the probability
function \(f(x) = 

$$
\begin{cases}
\frac{1}{B(\alpha,\beta)} x^{\alpha-1}(1-x)^{\beta-1}, & 0 < x < 1 \\ 0, & elsewhere
\end{cases}
$$

\) where \(B(\alpha,\beta) = \frac{\Gamma\alpha \Gamma\beta}{\Gamma(\alpha+\beta)}\)
Show that mean of X is \(\frac{\alpha}{\alpha+\beta}\) **(5 Marks)**
